          "title": "You'll want to know: shíjiān",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shíjiān — \"time; free time\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nǐ míngtiān yǒu shíjiān ma — Are you free tomorrow?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shíjiān is built from shí 'time' and jiān 'a gap', both inherited from Middle Chinese, dzyi and kean (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary glosses the first with another word for a time, and lists the second under an older form of the character."
            }
          ]
        },
